{"pagination":{"count":10,"page":1,"next_page":2,"total_count":1000,"total_pages":100},"records":[{"platform":"desktop","title":"Spacelab","url":"https://spacelab.co.uk","uuid":"de162c4d-f3e5-489f-b9eb-ac31b8e0412e","preview_url":"https://images.refero.design/styles/spacelab.co.uk/de162c4d-f3e5-489f-b9eb-ac31b8e0412e/preview_0.jpg","description":"A stark, gallery-like design system with a calm architectural sensibility. The interface sits on a bright white canvas with very large areas of negative space, making the few placed elements feel intentional and curated. Typography is the main visual structure: a single neutral sans-serif appears small, crisp, and highly legible, with a refined editorial restraint that feels precise rather than decorative. The brand mark is understated and lowercase, and the left-aligned vertical navigation reinforces the sense of order and quiet hierarchy.

Photography is the dominant visual feature, presented as a large, cleanly framed image block with sharp edges and minimal treatment. The imagery has a bright, high-key quality and a realistic, professional tone, echoing architectural interiors and spatial environments. There is little visible ornamentation, no heavy surface effects, and almost no chromatic variety beyond black text, soft gray secondary labels, and a muted violet-blue accent reserved for emphasis. Overall the style feels spacious, modern, disciplined, and quietly premium, with an architectural blueprint mood translated into a minimal contemporary layout."},{"platform":"desktop","title":"Studio Emmerer","url":"https://emmerer.com","uuid":"631b7cff-eb82-4962-9c72-e8fd2d3c1632","preview_url":"https://images.refero.design/styles/emmerer.com/631b7cff-eb82-4962-9c72-e8fd2d3c1632/preview_0.jpg","description":"Studio Emmerer has a stripped-back, architectural portfolio aesthetic that feels precise, editorial, and quietly rigorous. The visual language is built around stark contrast, flat white surfaces, thin horizontal rules, and an almost blueprint-like dependence on typography and spacing rather than ornament. The layout is open and linear, with a calm, measured rhythm: a text-led intro at the top, a large documentary-style project image beside it, and a long tabular project list below that gives the interface a catalog-like, archivist quality. Typography is clean and understated, with compact black text, small uppercase-like metadata labels in muted gray, and simple underlined text links that behave like functional annotations. The imagery is presented plainly and full-bleed within its frame, emphasizing built space, concrete textures, tunnels, and interiors with a cool, matter-of-fact presence. There are no decorative effects, gradients, shadows, or soft corners; the entire system feels sharp, minimal, and disciplined, like a contemporary architecture office site translated into a high-contrast print layout."},{"platform":"desktop","title":"19–86","url":"https://19-86.fr","uuid":"7a8c99db-5ce7-4fa4-b491-8f1fcac18991","preview_url":"https://images.refero.design/styles/19-86.fr/7a8c99db-5ce7-4fa4-b491-8f1fcac18991/preview_0.jpg","description":"Minimalist architectural-archive aesthetic with a stark black-and-white palette and a blueprint-like sense of precision. The screen feels almost printed rather than designed, with crisp 1px horizontal rules, tight tabular alignment, and a full-width list structure that creates a technical, document-like rhythm. The typography is very light and refined, using a clean sans-serif with restrained letter spacing that gives the text an orderly, engineered quality. The oversized “19-86” dominates the composition like a typographic monument, floating over the grid with dramatic scale but no visual weight beyond pure black ink. Small dot markers and thin dividers act as understated interface details, reinforcing the calm, exacting, diagrammatic mood. There is very little ornamental treatment: no color variation, no shadows, no softness, just spacious white fields, disciplined spacing, and an elegant, archival clarity that feels both modern and строго technical."},{"platform":"desktop","title":"IDHEAL","url":"https://idheal.fr","uuid":"195df59e-fc3b-448b-a4d8-ac075e1e990a","preview_url":"https://images.refero.design/styles/idheal.fr/195df59e-fc3b-448b-a4d8-ac075e1e990a/preview_0.jpg","description":"A stark, academic, monochrome editorial layout with a highly restrained visual language. The screen is dominated by oversized black typography on a pure white canvas, creating a serious, authoritative first impression. The logo-like heading feels bold, condensed, and architectural, acting as the primary visual anchor. Beneath it sits a large, uncropped photographic panel with a raw documentary quality, used sparingly as a visual break rather than decoration. The image is presented cleanly with no heavy treatment, letting natural color and real-world detail contrast against the strict black-and-white structure above. Overall spacing is tight and efficient, with a compact, text-led composition and minimal ornamentation. The aesthetic reads as institutional, design-conscious, and quietly modern, with sharp edges, flat surfaces, and an emphasis on typography, hierarchy, and disciplined restraint."},{"platform":"desktop","title":"V–A–C","url":"https://v-a-c.org/en","uuid":"ffef8672-f789-4329-8895-47e50f517d31","preview_url":"https://images.refero.design/styles/v-a-c.org/ffef8672-f789-4329-8895-47e50f517d31/preview_0.jpg","description":"A stark, editorial, architecture-inspired media interface built on a strict monochrome grid. The overall feeling is sparse, intellectual, and highly curated, with a white canvas, razor-thin black rules, and large areas of breathable negative space. Typography is the dominant visual device: clean, elegant sans-serif text in black, with a mix of compact labels and more expressive, slightly larger headlines that create a subtle hierarchy without ornament. The layout feels fixed and measured, organized into a disciplined multi-column system that reads almost like a catalog or museum index, with content blocks aligned precisely and spaced generously between sections. Imagery is used as raw documentary material rather than decoration: rectangular photos and film stills sit flat on the page with no rounded corners, shadows, or colored treatments, reinforcing the restrained, archival mood. Interactive elements are minimal and understated—simple text links, small navigation markers, thin rotated side labels, and quiet utility controls—blending into the grid instead of competing with it. The result is a refined, austere, contemporary cultural publishing aesthetic: precise, minimalist, and quietly premium, with an almost exhibition-like sense of order."},{"platform":"desktop","title":"Bibliothèque","url":"https://bibliothequedesign.com","uuid":"aab168d5-0658-459f-a7e5-23982b58a876","preview_url":"https://images.refero.design/styles/bibliothequedesign.com/aab168d5-0658-459f-a7e5-23982b58a876/preview_0.jpg","description":"A stark, monochrome editorial design with an almost gallery-like sense of restraint. The screen is dominated by a pure black canvas, creating a dramatic amount of negative space and an immediate feeling of focus and authority. Typography, where present, is minimal and understated, with a crisp white mark in the corner acting like a quiet signature rather than a full navigation system. The visual hierarchy is intentionally sparse, letting a single central image carry the page: a small, framed photograph floating in the darkness, presented with no visible chrome, no decorative treatment, and no competing interface noise. The overall composition feels full-bleed and immersive, yet disciplined, with a strong emphasis on contrast, silence, and editorial framing. The mood is refined, severe, and contemporary, closer to an art-book spread or minimalist design archive than a conventional digital interface. Flat surfaces, sharp edges, and the absence of color accents reinforce the austere black-and-white language, while the centered image placement gives the layout a calm, curated rhythm."},{"platform":"desktop","title":"Factory.ai","url":"https://factory.ai","uuid":"f1ed1d46-4e76-41fe-a9f8-3017e55dc6ee","preview_url":"https://images.refero.design/styles/factory.ai/f1ed1d46-4e76-41fe-a9f8-3017e55dc6ee/preview_0.jpg","description":"A stark, editorial technical-brutalist interface with a blueprint-like sense of order. The visual tone is minimal, precise, and highly engineered: a pale white-gray canvas, crisp black typography, and faint cool-gray rules create a clean architectural structure. The layout feels spacious but disciplined, with a centered content column, strong left-aligned text blocks, and carefully balanced two-column compositions that pair dense copy with restrained product visuals. Typography is the dominant design feature: large Geist headlines with tight letter-spacing give the page a compressed, intentional presence, while smaller body copy and monospace code blocks reinforce the software-development atmosphere. Buttons and tags are compact and functional, mostly outlined or filled in neutral tones, with rounded corners kept subtle and consistent. The only vivid color is a small orange accent used sparingly for badges, status dots, and tiny indicators, which cuts through the monochrome field like a technical marker. Imagery is abstract and utilitarian—dotted motifs, wireframe-like frames, CLI panels, and UI screenshots—presented with lots of breathing room and little decorative flourish. Overall it feels like a refined developer-tool landing experience: quiet, analytical, modern, and exacting, with an architectural precision that prioritizes clarity over ornament."},{"platform":"desktop","title":"Workflow","url":"https://www.workflow.design","uuid":"fcfc37c8-7cbc-4440-9e0f-94ca9e8c4a72","preview_url":"https://images.refero.design/styles/www.workflow.design/fcfc37c8-7cbc-4440-9e0f-94ca9e8c4a72/preview_0.jpg","description":"A restrained, editorial-style SaaS landing page with an architectural blueprint feel on a bright white marble-like canvas. The visual tone is airy, precise, and understated, relying on generous whitespace, centered composition, and a clean grid to create a calm sense of order. Typography is the main character: a refined serif headline gives the hero and section titles a quiet premium presence, while the rest of the interface uses a crisp functional sans-serif for navigation, labels, and body text. The palette stays almost entirely monochrome, with soft off-white section shifts, pale gray surfaces, and thin hairline borders used to separate content instead of heavy shadows or bold color blocks. Buttons are subtle and ghost-like, with light fills and minimal contrast, and the overall hierarchy is communicated through spacing, alignment, and type scale rather than decoration. Screenshots and content previews are placed inside soft-edged cards with rounded corners, lightly framed and carefully contained, reinforcing the product’s polished, design-tool aesthetic. The result feels minimal but not sterile: sophisticated, quiet, and highly intentional, with a modern studio-grade professionalism."},{"platform":"desktop","title":"Waka Waka","url":"https://wakawaka.world","uuid":"dbfdd355-b07e-40d6-9571-09284475794c","preview_url":"https://images.refero.design/styles/wakawaka.world/dbfdd355-b07e-40d6-9571-09284475794c/preview_0.jpg","description":"Waka Waka has a stark, editorial poster aesthetic with a refined gallery-wall sensibility. The composition is built around a centered, narrow off-white canvas that feels like a printed sheet pinned to a larger neutral field, giving the whole interface an artifact-like presence. Oversized black typography dominates the layout, especially the monumental Waka headlines, which are set with heavy weight and tight spacing to create a bold, almost magazine-cover impact. The visual hierarchy is driven by scale and whitespace rather than color or decoration, resulting in a disciplined, grid-based rhythm that feels curated and deliberate.

Photography is treated as the main visual counterpoint to type: isolated product shots of furniture, cropped tightly and placed in clean rectangular blocks with sharp edges. The images are quiet, studio-like, and monochromatic, reinforcing the restrained palette and print-forward mood. Small text labels and minimal navigation sit lightly at the edges, nearly disappearing into the overall composition, while the generous negative space keeps the layout airy despite the strong typographic presence. The surface treatment is flat and matte, with no visible rounding, shadows, or ornamental effects, which strengthens the crisp, contemporary editorial tone. Overall it feels premium, restrained, and highly art-directed, like a design catalog translated into a modern digital presentation."},{"platform":"desktop","title":"Co Projects","url":"https://co-projects.xyz","uuid":"f404451e-34c6-4762-83bf-93e4e2885b02","preview_url":"https://images.refero.design/styles/co-projects.xyz/f404451e-34c6-4762-83bf-93e4e2885b02/preview_0.jpg","description":"A stark, gallery-wall style light interface built around extreme typographic scale and abstract geometric branding. The screen is almost entirely white, creating a clean canvas with a contemplative, editorial feel, while oversized black circular letterforms dominate the composition like monumental art pieces. The visual language is highly minimal and architectural: hard edges, precise alignment, and a subtle vertical divider introduce structure without softness or ornament. Navigation is tiny and restrained, sitting quietly at the top edge, which makes the massive central graphics feel even more emphatic. Typography appears crisp and modern, with a compact, academic tone and very little hierarchy beyond scale. The overall aesthetic is monochrome, austere, and concept-driven, with strong contrast, generous negative space, and a polished, poster-like presence."}]}
